# Cloudflare Pages _redirects file
#
# Pretty-URL the embed endpoint. The page lives at /embed.html on disk
# (so it can be served as a static file with no server-side logic), but
# the public URL is /embed?url=… — extension-less, matching the
# moviplayer.com/embed pattern.
#
# Why NO /embed.html rule? The previous deployment had a line
# `/embed.html  /embed.html 200` meant to "break a redirect loop". It
# actually CAUSED the loop: Cloudflare's _redirects parser matched
# that rule for any request to /embed.html, then tried to rewrite to
# /embed.html — which Cloudflare normalises to /embed (it strips
# trailing .html on its own asset-serving path), which matched the
# `/embed → /embed.html` rule again → infinite 308 redirect.
#
# The fix: ONLY have the `/embed → /embed.html` rule. Cloudflare's
# static-asset serving already handles /embed.html directly (it's a
# real file on disk), so it never enters the redirect pipeline.
# The `/embed` request (no extension) gets rewritten to /embed.html
# internally, no second hop.
#
# Status 200 = rewrite (URL stays as /embed in the address bar).
# Status 301/302/308 = redirect (URL changes, breaks iframe URLs).
/embed  /embed.html  200
/e      /embed.html  200
/v      /embed.html  200
/watch  /embed.html  200
